      ":question/id": "fdc72af0-d487-506c-acc9-d5689d1b3071",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=0$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)=-1$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x+\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)-\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)-\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
